//- Settings and folders. Params: d.
div(data-ui="prose")
  raw p("The studio reads its settings from environment variables when it starts. Set one for a single run by putting it before the command (`PORT=8800 npm run studio`), or in your shell's profile. Voice settings may also go in a git-ignored `.env` file at the repository root. After changing a setting, restart the studio.")

  h2#settings Environment variables
  div(role="region" aria-label="Environment variables" tabindex="0")
    table
      thead
        tr
          th Variable
          th Default
          th Meaning
      tbody
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_DATA`")
          td
            raw md("`./data`")
          td The data directory: the database, thumbnails, files, caches and renders. This studio uses the folder shown below.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`PORT`, `HOST`")
          td 8787, 127.0.0.1
          td
            raw md("Where the studio listens. Any address other than loopback (`HOST=0.0.0.0`, a network address) is refused unless `STUDIO_TOKEN` is set. See [Open the studio to other devices](#network).")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_TOKEN`")
          td none
          td
            raw md("A secret of at least 16 characters. When it is set, every page asks for it once (a sign-in cookie keeps it for 30 days) and every API request must carry the cookie or `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Required for any `HOST` other than loopback.")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`FFMPEG_PATH`")
          td
            raw md("`ffmpeg` on the `PATH`")
          td FFmpeg, when it is not on the PATH. On Windows a winget install is found automatically.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_RENDER_WORKERS`")
          td CPU cores − 2, at most 8
          td
            raw md("Threads that draw frames. A single render can ask for its own (1 to 16).")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_FOOTAGE_CACHE_MB`")
          td 512
          td Memory for decoded footage frames, per process.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_AUTHOR`")
          td
            raw md("`studio-user` (web), `mcp-client` (MCP)")
          td
            raw md("Recorded as the author of what a process writes. The repository's `.mcp.json` sets `claude-code`.")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_TOOLS`")
          td all tools
          td For an MCP server process: a comma-separated list of the only tools it offers.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_RUNNER`")
          td on
          td
            raw md("For an MCP server process: `0` means it does not pick up queued renders.")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_REPO`")
          td this checkout
          td
            raw md("The repository `export_clip` writes to and `import_clip` reads from.")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_CLAUDE_BIN`")
          td
            raw md("`claude` on the `PATH`")
          td The Claude Code command that Run now starts. Without one, the Run now button is hidden.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_AGENT_TIMEOUT`")
          td 600
          td Seconds a Run now session may take.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`STUDIO_KOKORO_DIR`, `STUDIO_TTS`, `STUDIO_WHISPER_CLI`, `STUDIO_WHISPER_MODEL`, `STUDIO_WHISPER_MODEL_2`, `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`")
          td
          td
            raw md("Voice and transcription: see [Set up voice and transcription](/docs/sound#voice-setup).")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`CHROME`")
          td found automatically
          td The Chrome program for the browser parity test and the recording and measuring scripts.

  h2#network Open the studio to other devices
  raw p("By default the studio answers only on this computer (`127.0.0.1`), with no password, and only to the names `localhost`, `127.0.0.1` and `[::1]`. To open it from a phone or another computer on your network, give it a token and an address:")
  pre
    code
      | STUDIO_TOKEN=<a long random secret> HOST=0.0.0.0 npm run studio
  raw p("Then open `http://<this computer's address>:8787` on the other device and enter the token. Without a token the studio refuses to start on such an address, and a token shorter than 16 characters is refused too. Every page, the API, the media and the share links then need the token; the sign-in cookie is `HttpOnly` and `SameSite=Lax`.")
  +callout(variant="warning")
    @content
      raw p("**The studio speaks plain HTTP.** On a network you do not trust, put it behind a reverse proxy that adds HTTPS (Caddy, nginx) or reach it through an SSH tunnel; otherwise the token travels in the clear. The studio runs asset code you or Claude wrote, so never open it to people you would not let run code on this computer. To share a clip with anyone, export it and publish the folder instead: see [Share a clip as a link](/docs/share).")

  h2#data-directory The data directory
  raw p("This studio keeps its data in `" + d.live.dataDir + "`. Git ignores it. Inside:")
  div(role="region" aria-label="Data directory" tabindex="0")
    table
      thead
        tr
          th Path
          th Holds
      tbody
        tr
          td
            raw md("`studio.db`")
          td The library, clips, renders, requests and events: one SQLite database.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`thumbs/`, `files/`")
          td Asset thumbnails and filmstrips; uploaded files, fonts, footage and baked sequences.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`cache/`, `frames/`")
          td Mixed audio and other caches; stills drawn for the checks and for Claude.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`renders/`")
          td Every render's MP4, poster, captions, report, sheets and credits.
  raw p("To back up your work, stop the studio and copy this folder. To start a fresh library, point `STUDIO_DATA` at an empty folder. Never edit `studio.db` by hand while a studio or an MCP server is using it.")

  h2#repository The repository
  div(role="region" aria-label="Repository folders" tabindex="0")
    table
      thead
        tr
          th Folder
          th Holds
      tbody
        tr
          td
            raw md("`assets/`")
          td
            raw md("The source of every function asset, one flat folder (`name.v2.js` is version 2 of `name`).")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`clips/<clip>/`")
          td
            raw md("One folder per clip: `compose.mjs` builds its composition, `clip.json` is its export.")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`library/`")
          td
            raw md("The content store exported clips share: `versions/`, `sources/`, `files/<sha256>`.")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`showcase/`")
          td The recipe and the recorded steps that rebuild the twelve showcase clips, with their pictures, recordings and voice takes.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`work/<clip>/`")
          td Notes, checks and sheets of clips made through the motion process. Its pictures and sounds stay out of git.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`fonts/`, `vendor/lucide/`")
          td The bundled fonts with their licences; the icon set kit-icon draws.
        tr
          td
            raw md("`src/`")
          td
            raw md("The studio: `core` (the asset runtime shared by Node and the browser), `render`, `studio`, `mcp`, `server`, `ui`, `player` (the share page and the live session of an interactive clip) and `docs` (this manual).")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`docs/`")
          td
            raw md("`ASSET_CONTRACT.md`, `COOKBOOK.md` and the showcase evidence.")
        tr
          td
            raw md("`output/`")
          td
            raw md("Exports and evidence from the scripts, and `output/share/<clip>/`, each clip's share folder (ignored by git).")
  raw p("No video is ever committed: renders go on GitHub releases. The pages of this manual are templates in `src/docs/templates/`, drawn by the studio's server with Faqir UI.")
